# Data conversion between bit and byte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and byte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.125B with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.1875B; backward, converting 1B to 8b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5B yields 12.0b.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(B))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(B))
backward_whole: int = 1B
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.125B
0.1875B
8b
12.0b

<<< stderr
